alist at the 1983 World Championships and was expected to represent the US in Los Angeles. He lost out controversially in the US Trials, however, against " [:a {:href "/athletes/60692"} "Randy Lewis"] ", with the decision going to the courts, and then requiring a re-match between the two wrestlers. Lewis had been a member of the ill-fated 1980 US Olympic team. In Los Angeles he won Group B, going through without a loss, and then met Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/58984"} "Kosei Akaishi"] ", who had unusually advanced despite losing a match in Group A, in the final. Lewis had been dominant throughout and crushed Akaishi in the second period of the gold medal match, with the bout stopped on technical superiority with Lewis leading 24-11."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Round Eliminated"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "263"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60692"} "Randy Lewis"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "128"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58984"} "Kosei Akaishi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "157"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/59207"} "Lee Jeong-Geun"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/count